1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Speaker 1] Yes, you have made several videos. The effort you have put in is truly commendable.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The points you have stated regarding Advaitins and Mayavadis are correct.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The way you have presented and refuted those schools of thought, that sequence is also good. I am not denying it.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
But regarding your presentation of the Dvaita school, you made a video explaining the 'Sharira-Shariri Bhava' (body-soul relation).

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
In that video, there is a scriptural sentence that says, "He whose body is the earth" (Yasya Prithvi Shariram).

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
While explaining that, you say Madhvas only accept Him as the efficient cause (Nimitta Karana), and that God is not the material cause (Upadana Karana).

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Yes, God is indeed not the material cause of this world; He is solely the efficient cause.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
However, God has a distinct body of His own. It is a body of pure knowledge and bliss (Jnana-Anandatmaka).

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Why should the earth be God's body? God dwells in all of us—who are material, sentient, and insentient...

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:25,000
...as the inner controller (Antaryami) through His own distinct, divine body, and He inspires us from within. That is the only meaning of that scriptural text.

11
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
God has a distinct body of pure knowledge and bliss.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Why should material nature (Prakriti) be God's body? Prakriti is Prakriti.

13
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:46,000
God's body is of the very nature of God Himself. We do not postulate any difference between God's eyes, His feet, or His actions.

14
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:56,000
For this reason, God, through His own infinite forms, pervades this entire universe in infinite ways.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Because He is all-pervading, we interpret the scriptures in this way.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:15,000
All the material-cause scriptural texts (Upadana Shrutis) you have quoted are interpreted in this sense: He pervades everything as the inner controller.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,000
He pervades with His own divine body, and not that someone else's body becomes God's body. Because God's body is entirely distinct.

18
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:32,000
How can your body or our body become His? Or how can anyone else's body become His? We do not accept that kind of body-soul relationship.

19
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:44,000
If we were to say that all the various bodies of different creatures in this living world are God's body...

20
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:53,000
...then there are so many sinful births. We humans have countless flaws and defects in us.

21
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Since we possess countless defects, this world cannot possibly be God's body.

22
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,000
God's body is entirely distinct, made of pure knowledge and bliss.

23
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:20,000
It has absolutely no connection to material nature (Prakriti).

24
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,000
There is no connection between this world and God's divine body.

25
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Therefore, even though God is perfect with infinite auspicious attributes and free of all defects, He exists as the inner controller.

26
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Now, let's take a car as an example. What we say is that God has a form of His own, in fact, many forms, infinite forms.

27
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:51,000
You know the concept of 'Navanari Kunjara' (nine women forming an elephant) and 'Panchanari Turaga' (five women forming a horse), right?

28
00:03:51,000 --> 00:04:05,000
If nine women stand in a specific posture, it forms an elephant, or five women form a horse—you are familiar with this.

29
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:12,000
In this manner, God gives form to objects.

30
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:24,000
If you ask how God exists in this car, He exists in the form of the car, but as His own distinct form. There is no connection between inert matter and God. It remains a form of pure knowledge and bliss.

31
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
If you take the scriptural statement 'Dvaa Suparnaa' (two birds), how is it explained?

32
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:38,000
There is no body-soul (Sharira-Shariri) relation between the individual soul (Jiva) and Brahman. They are entirely distinct.

33
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:45,000
They have distinct bodies and distinct essential natures. There is no difference between God's eyes, His limbs, and God Himself.

34
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:52,000
There is no difference; there is no distinction between His attributes, His form, and His actions. In Dvaita philosophy, they are all one.

35
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:58,000
The individual soul (Jiva) is entirely distinct. Even among the liberated souls, they remain distinct.

36
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:05,000
All liberated souls are regarded as servants of the Supreme Lord. Even in liberation, we have a system of hierarchy (Taratamya).

37
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:11,000
There is no equality in liberation; there is no equality in bliss (Ananda).

38
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Therefore, God's body has an entirely separate system.

39
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:31,000
God carries out His activities through His own distinct forms, and He is the cause of this world's creation, sustenance, control, etc.

40
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:39,000
He does not take on this material, inert body.

41
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:53,000
To be even clearer, the divine incarnations like Rama and Krishna, or forms like Srinivasa, do not possess a body of flesh and blood.

42
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Even if one tries to cut or dissect God's body, no material, physical elements (Panchabhoutika elements) will ever be found in it.

43
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:08,000
It is purely a distinct body.

44
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:15,000
It is completely different from material nature, highly exalted. There is no content of Prakriti (matter) within it.

45
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Explained in this sense, God is the inner controller (Antaryami), and He is the inner controller through His own divine body, which is His very essence.

46
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[Speaker 2] What you said is good, you have presented it well.

47
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:38,000
I, too, am familiar with the Madhva philosophy, so it seems there is no error in my understanding of it.

48
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:46,000
I recall it being stated similarly in the video as well. Did I say something wrong, or did I say something contrary to it? I don't think so.

49
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Be that as it may, regarding these scriptural texts (Shrutis), you seem to override the scripture with human logic (Yukti).

50
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:06,000
You argue that under no circumstance can this flawed material nature be God's body, and that it is contrary to logic.

51
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:13,000
But human logic is not competent enough to override the scriptural text (Shruti).

52
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Therefore, our position is that we must accept the Shruti as it is, which proclaims the body-soul relationship between the soul and the Supreme Soul.

53
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Regarding the incarnations like Rama and Krishna, we say exactly what you said.

54
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:51,000
We agree that His form is not an idol made of inert material nature, but is of the nature of pure knowledge and is transcendental (Alaukika). There is no dispute about that.

55
00:07:52,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Furthermore, what we refer to as the body-soul (Sharira-Shariri) relationship, you also express using terms like 'inner controller state', 'control', etc.

56
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:13,000
But you hesitate to explicitly state that there is a 'Sharira-Shariri' relationship, that's all.

57
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:21,000
It is merely a difference of terminology; there is no difference in the core meaning. Therefore, it seems to me that on this doctrinal point, there is no real dispute between us and the Madhvas.

58
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:29,000
[Speaker 1] When you explain the body-soul relationship, you describe it as a 'transformation' (Parinama).

59
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:34,000
We are not talking about transformation here. God never undergoes transformation.

60
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:44,000
He does not transform; God remains uniformly present everywhere in His own divine body. The eternally singular Vaikuntha Narayana Himself manifests as the forms of Rama, Krishna, etc.

61
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Even the Bimba forms (source/archetype forms) within you and me possess the same power as Narayana Himself—we refer to them as Bimba forms, and that Bimba form is distinct.

62
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:05,000
We hold that this Bimba form is Narayana Himself. The Jivas are different; they depend on God and remain forever His servants.

63
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:15,000
They remain His servants, and we say Prakriti (matter) is subordinate to God in this sense. We do not speak of it in terms of 'transformation'.

64
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:22,000
[Speaker 2] But you say that the state of Prakriti (material nature) changes, right? That is exactly what we say too.

65
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:37,000
What we propose is not the transformation of God's essential nature (Svaroopa Parinamavada), but the transformation of His attributes (Visheshana Parinamavada) or the transformation of His body (Sharira Parinamavada). Even on this matter, it is merely a difference of words; there is no difference in the core meaning.
